WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.810
Now imagine yourself working as a front end web developer.

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:08.248
You've just gotten a design from your company's graphic designer and

00:00:08.248 --> 00:00:12.800
you now need to take this image or PDF file and turn it into a website with

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:18.250
all the necessary components, HTML files, CSS files, and JavaScript files.

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:18.820
&gt;&gt; Yep.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:22.665
But how do you translate that visual design into an actual website, right?

00:00:22.665 --> 00:00:24.270
And, where do you start?

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:25.460
What decisions do you need to make?

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:26.105
What do you need to know?

00:00:26.105 --> 00:00:28.730
&gt;&gt; Mm-hm. &gt;&gt; And these are like excellent questions to ask.

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:32.020
But before we do that, we should probably build a good conceptual understanding

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:33.070
of the way websites work.

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:34.250
&gt;&gt; Yep, exactly.

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:38.010
So, you can think of a website much like your house.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:41.740
HTML files are like the structure where the wall's placed.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:43.310
What room is your livingroom?

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:44.220
What room is your kitchen?

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:45.340
Which room is your bedroom?

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:49.700
CSS files are then the style of your house.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:50.870
What color is the carpeting?

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:52.630
What decorations do you have up?

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:53.859
What color are the walls?

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:59.890
JavaScript files are then your interactive components.

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:04.300
You can think of them like your garage door opener, or your television remote.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:06.530
They're changing some element of your house.

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:11.100
Now much like there are rules for how things in your house behave,

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:14.350
you can't have a television that's just floating on the wall.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:16.400
It has to be attached by something.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:19.600
There are also rules for how websites behave.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:21.350
The same goes for tools.

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:24.840
You can't put together a bookshelf, for example, without a screwdriver.

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:28.470
And there are also many web tools available to help you build your websites.

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:29.730
&gt;&gt; Yeah, that's a great point.

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:31.250
I love this analogy, it's an awesome analogy.

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:34.250
What do you say we get started in learning some of the basics?

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:34.770
&gt;&gt; Sounds great.

